The first is "sea".
The second is "eat".
The firstlength is the number of characters in first.
The secondlength is the number of characters in second.
The width is secondlength plus 1.
The height is firstlength plus 1.
The cells is height times width.
The chart is a list of 16 zeros.
For every row from 1 to firstlength.
For every column from 1 to secondlength.
The above is row minus 1.
The before is column minus 1.
The letter is the slice of first from above to above plus 1.
The other is the slice of second from before to before plus 1.
The spot is row times width plus column.
The corner is above times width plus before.
If letter matches other, set item spot of chart to item corner of chart plus 1.
If letter does not match other.
The up is above times width plus column.
The left is row times width plus before.
The best is item up of chart.
If item left of chart is more than best, set best to item left of chart.
Set item spot of chart to best.

The common is firstlength times width plus secondlength.
The shared is item common of chart.
The answer is firstlength plus secondlength minus 2 times shared.
Show answer.
